      <activity id="3191c92d-2444-5fb7-971b-4e4d7990b0a9" activityNameId="e0d73cb5-1bee-5c55-be61-7d4d02bd527a" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Ethyl acetate from butane, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Ethyl acetate from butane, at plant
The multioutput-process "formic acid production, butane oxidation process"  delivers the co-products formic acid, methyl acetate, ethyl acetate, acetic acid, methyl ethyl ketone, and acetone. The allocation is based on mass balance.;
UUID: b56ec353-1236-35ad-a237-eb0ea6fc35a6
Butane oxidation including materials, energy uses, infrastructure and emissions.
Location: The inventory is modelled for Europe.
Technology: Oxidation of butane
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature data 
Extrapolations: Transports and emissions are modelled with standard methods.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_b56ec353-1236-35ad-a237-eb0ea6fc35a6.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
